.SH NAME
kc-vault-purge - Destroy a soft-deleted vault for good


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkc vault purge [NAME] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes an archived vault permanently, history included. With --expired it
purges every archived vault past the retention window instead.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--expired\fP[=false]
	purge every archived vault past the retention window

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for purge


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--vault\fP=""
	target vault (overrides active vault)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBkc-vault(1)\fP
